  OWASP Dependency-Check suppression file.

  Add CVEs here ONLY with justification and a re-evaluation date.
  Each suppression MUST include:
    - The CVE identifier (or CPE for false-positive CPE matches)
    - A <notes> element explaining WHY the CVE does not apply to this project
    - A re-evaluation date (when the suppression should be reviewed)

  See https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html
-->
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">

    <!--
      CPE false positive: dependency-check matches `androidx.sqlite:sqlite-*`
      to `cpe:/a:sqlite:sqlite`, but androidx.sqlite is a thin Kotlin wrapper
      over the SQLite engine that ships in the Android OS. The C SQLite
      library is managed by the platform (per-device Android version), not
      by this artifact — every CVE in the matched CPE applies to that
      bundled library and is patched by the OS vendor, not by us.

      Suppress the entire CPE match (which surfaces ~25 SQLite CVEs per
      androidx.sqlite artifact, all the same false positive).

      Re-evaluate: 2027-06-01 (annual review).
    -->
    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[
            False positive: androidx.sqlite is a Kotlin wrapper, not the
            C SQLite engine. SQLite CVEs apply to the Android-OS-bundled
            engine, patched by the platform. Re-evaluate 2027-06-01.
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/androidx\.sqlite/.*$</packageUrl>
        <cpe>cpe:/a:sqlite:sqlite</cpe>
    </suppress>

    <!--
      CVE-2024-7254 — protobuf-java recursion DoS on untrusted input.
      The hit is on a *shaded* protobuf-javalite 3.21.8 inside the
      `inspector.jar` packed in androidx.work:work-runtime-2.9.1.aar.
      That inspector.jar is loaded only by Android Studio's WorkManager
      Inspector during debugging — it is never reached at production
      runtime. We also never parse attacker-supplied protobuf bytes; the
      only protobuf payloads in the app are WorkManager's own internal
      Room-backed state.

      Suppress by sha1 of the shaded inspector jar (work-runtime 2.9.1)
      so a future androidx.work bump invalidates the suppression and
      forces re-evaluation. Also re-evaluate: 2027-06-01.
    -->
    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[
            Shaded protobuf-javalite inside work-runtime-2.9.1's
            debug-only inspector.jar; not reachable at production runtime
            and we never parse untrusted protobuf. Re-evaluate 2027-06-01
            or whenever work-runtime is bumped.
        ]]></notes>
        <filePath regex="true">.*work-runtime-2\.9\.1\.aar.*inspector\.jar.*</filePath>
        <cve>CVE-2024-7254</cve>
    </suppress>

</suppressions>
